              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "141.742", "xlink:href" => "#cvHcT4mHDxS-yN7A3RsifSanDgY=-glyph-5-1", :y => "87.58"}
              %g{:fill => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "fill-opacity" => "1"}
                %use{:x => "145.34575", "xlink:href" => "#cvHcT4mHDxS-yN7A3RsifSanDgY=-glyph-4-6", :y => "88.96375"}
            %p
              Consider then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of the total bottom morphism along the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_2
              of the other summand. Since pullbacks of isomorphisms are isomorphisms, the resulting top left object must be (isomorphic to)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+law"} pasting law
              this pullback factors into two pullback squares, as shown above. But the pullback on the right gives the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+coproducts"} coproducts are disjoint
              in an extensive category (see
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "extensive+category#DisjointAndPullbackStableCoproducts"} here
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2 \to \varnothing
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+initial+objects"} strict initial objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo ∅
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_2 \simeq \varnothing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
              cannot be an initial object, since otherwise
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              would be too, which it is not by assumption of connectedness (Rem.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InitialObjectIsNotConnected"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊔
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \simeq X_1 \sqcup X_2
              is initial.
            %p
              In the other direction, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has non non-trivial coproduct decomposition and consider any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                    %mo +
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y + Z
              into a coproduct. By
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensivity
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "extensive+category#eq:HomIntoCoproductIsPullbackIfDomainIsCoproduct"} here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = U + V
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \coloneqq f^\ast(i_Y)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \coloneqq f^\ast(i_Z)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is initial, meaning that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              factors through either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              belongs to exactly one of the two subsets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo +
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(X, Y) \hookrightarrow \hom(X, Y + Z)
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo +
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(X, Z) \hookrightarrow \hom(X, Y + Z)
          %h3#general_properties General properties
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of connected objects over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+category"} connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              is itself a connected object.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Because coproducts in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              commute with
              %em limits
              of connected diagrams.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Ob(C)
              is connected and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is connected.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Certainly
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is not
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+initial+object"} strict
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = U + V
              (see prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InExtensiveCategoryCOnnectedObjectsArePrimitiveUnderCoproduct"}
              above), so that we have an epimorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to U + V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_U: U \hookrightarrow U + V
              is epic, in fact an epic equalizer of two maps
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 2
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                      %mi V
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi U
                      %mo +
                      %mi V
                      %mo +
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U + i_1, U + i_2: U + V \rightrightarrows U + V + V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_U
              is an isomorphism; by disjointness of coproducts, this forces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              to be initial. Of course
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is not initial; otherwise
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              would be initial.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              It need not be the case that products of connected objects are connected. For example, in the topos
              = succeed "-Set," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}
              decomposes as a countable coproduct of copies of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive topos
          %p
            We do have the following partial result, generalizing the case of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
          #prod.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a cocomplete
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times (-) : C \to C
              preserve
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              In the first place,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is connected. For suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = U + V
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is not initial. The two coproduct inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo +
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to U + U
              are distinct by disjointness of sums. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is a separator, there must be a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to U
              separating these inclusions. We then conclude
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \cong 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≅
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \cong 0
              by disjointness of sums.
            %p
              Now let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              be connected. The two inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mn 2
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_1, i_2: X \to X + X
              are distinct, so there exists a point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon 1 \to X
              separating them. For each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \colon 1 \to Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi y
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_y = (X \times y) \cup (a \times Y)
              is connected (we define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_y
              to be a sum of connected objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \times Y
              amalgamated over the connected object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ×
                      %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \times y = 1 \times 1 = 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: \bigcup_{y \colon 1 \to Y} T_y \to X \times Y
            %p
              where the union is again a sum of connected objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_y
              amalgamated over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \times Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is epic, because the evident map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{y \colon 1 \to Y} X \times y \cong X \times \sum_{y \colon 1 \to Y} 1 \to X \times Y
            %p
              is epic (by the assumptions that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separator"} separator
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times -
              preserves epis), and this map factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is also connected.
          #prod2.num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              The same method of proof shows that for an arbitrary family of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+spaces"} connected spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_\alpha\}_{\alpha \in A}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = (x_\alpha)
              in the product space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \prod_{\alpha \in A} X_\alpha
              contains at least all those points which differ from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              in at most finitely many coordinates. However, the set of such points is dense in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{\alpha \in A} X_\alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{\alpha \in A} X_\alpha
              must also be connected.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Connected objects in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
                are precisely
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+spaces"} connected topological spaces
            %li
              %p
                For a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
                of
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
                = succeed "-sets." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                Objects in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
                are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                of connected objects.
              %p
                (This includes categories such as
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"} permutation representations
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
                is connected as a scheme (which by definition means that its underlying topological space is connected) if and only if it is connected as an object of the category of schemes. See
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://gausyu.github.io/MathBlog/2016/02/13/Connectedness-of-Schemes/"} here
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+graph"} connected graph
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"}> connected topos
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+coproduct"} disjoint coproduct
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct-preserving+representable"} coproduct-preserving representable
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} n-connected object in an (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Connected objects were called
            %em abstractly exclusively unary objects
            in:
          %ul
            %li#Bunge66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marta+Bunge"}> Marta Bunge
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/Bunge-CategoriesOfSetValuedFunctors.pdf#page=47"} p. 32
              of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categories of set valued functors
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bunge-CategoriesOfSetValuedFunctors.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and were called
            %em Z-objects
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf-E.+Hoffmann"}> Rudolf-E. Hoffmann
              \:
              = succeed "." do
                %em A categorical concept of connectedness
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers"} Cahiers
              XIV-2 (1973) 34-35 &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Hoffmann-Connectedness.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=CTGDC_1973__14_2_153_0"} numdam:CTGDC_1973__14_2_153_0
          %p
            and
            %em coprime objects
            in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reinhard+B%C3%B6rger"}> Reinhard Börger
              ,
              %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/81149450.pdf#page=10"} p. 136
              of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multicoreflective subcategories and coprime objects
              %strong 33
              2 (1989) 127-142 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/81149450.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
          %p
            Last revised on May 25, 2024 at 15:30:00.
